course: dictionary
lesson: 7452
title: Many meanings of pool
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. «Pool rules are about slipping, pushing, drains and never swimming without a grown-up watching.» The rules are about swimming, so pool means a place filled with water to swim in.
explain: «Walking sharks can survive for hours with very little oxygen when a rock pool gets warm and stale at low tide.» Low tide is the clue. A rock pool is a small pool of sea water left among rocks when the tide goes out. «Wet pool edges are slippery, so you should walk, not run.» Slippery and walk, not run, tell you that pool here means water, not a game.
explain: Pool can also be a verb. If someone says, «Let's pool our money and buy a present», they mean put money together so everyone can share it. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
fact: A pool is a place filled with water to swim in, or a small area of liquid such as a pool of rainwater.
fact: «Pool rules are about slipping, pushing, drains and never swimming without a grown-up watching.»
fact: A rock pool is a small pool of sea water left among rocks when the tide goes out.
fact: To pool is to put money or things together so everyone can share them.
fact: A car pool is a group of people who share car journeys, and pool is also a game played with balls and a stick on a table.
exercise: «Pool rules are about slipping, pushing, drains and never swimming without a grown-up watching.» In this sentence, what is a pool? | A small puddle of rain on the path | *A place filled with water to swim in | A game played with balls and a stick
exercise: «Walking sharks can survive for hours when a rock pool gets warm and stale at low tide.» What is a rock pool? | *A small pool of sea water left among rocks when the tide goes out | A deep hole dug in the sand | A tank for fish in a shop
exercise: Mia says, «We will pool our pocket money and buy one big present.» What does pool mean? | Play a game with a stick | Swim in the sea | Spill water on the floor | *Put money together so everyone can share
test: «There was a pool of rainwater on the path.» What does pool mean here? | A place to swim in | *A small area of liquid | A group of cars
test: Dad joined a car pool so friends take turns to drive to school. What is a car pool here? | A swimming lesson | A game played with balls | A puddle on the road | *A group of people sharing car journeys
exam: «The sun made a pool of light on the floor.» What does pool mean? | *A small area of light, like a pool of liquid spread on the floor | A game played on a table with a stick | To put money together | A place filled with water to swim in
